    "title": "Article 70: Discharge of President's Functions in Other Contingencies",
    "definition": "Parliament may make such provisions as it thinks fit for the discharge of the functions of the President in any contingency not provided for in this Chapter.",
    "explanation": "Article 70 is a residuary provision empowering Parliament to legislate for situations where neither the President nor the Vice-President is available to discharge presidential functions — for example, if both offices are simultaneously vacant, or if the Vice-President is also incapacitated. This provision has not yet been invoked, as India has never faced such a contingency, but it ensures constitutional continuity in extreme circumstances.",
